Reactive power cannot be transferred through a DC link. Hence, the reactive power requirements of the converter stations must be supplied locally by the connected AC systems. The rectifier consumes reactive power from the AC system connected to it, while the inverter supplies reactive power to the AC system connected to it. Therefore, the correct statement is: \[\boxed{
\shortstack[c]{
\text{(B) The rectifier consumes reactive power and the inverter supplies reactive power}\\
\text{from/to the respective connected AC systems}
}
}\]

