=
\frac{\text{Operating coil current}}
{\text{Restraining coil current}}\] The operating torque is \[T_O=K(i_1-i_2)n_o\] and the restraining torque is \[T_R=
K\left(
\frac{n_r}{2}i_1+
\frac{n_r}{2}i_2
\right)
=
K\left(
\frac{i_1+i_2}{2}
\right)n_r\] At balance, \[T_O=T_R\] \[K(i_1-i_2)n_o
=
K\left(
\frac{i_1+i_2}{2}
\right)n_r\] \[\frac{n_r}{n_o}
=
\frac{(i_1-i_2)}
{\left(\dfrac{i_1+i_2}{2}\right)}\] The quantity \[\frac{(i_1-i_2)}
{\left(\dfrac{i_1+i_2}{2}\right)}\] is the ratio of operating current to restraining current, which is defined as the relay bias. Hence, \[\text{Bias}
